course: dictionary
lesson: 12320
title: Corrugated: ridges that make things strong
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Corrugated is an adjective. It describes a surface with lots of ridges and grooves in rows, like waves. You will find it on metal roofs and in cardboard boxes. Look at the words around it: a roof, a box, or a road tells you which kind of corrugated is meant. «The shed roof was made of corrugated iron.»
explain: Ridges are the raised lines and grooves are the dips between them. When a flat sheet is folded into lines like this, it becomes much stiffer and stronger, so it can hold weight without bending. That is why builders and box-makers use this shape.
explain: Corrugated can also describe a face. «Dad's forehead was corrugated with worry.» Here it means wrinkled into lines, like a frown. The same word can describe a shape or a face, so read the whole sentence to decide.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Our parcel arrived in a corrugated cardboard box» still makes sense if you think of a box with ridges in its card. If your meaning fits, you are right.
fact: Corrugated means shaped into ridges and grooves, like waves.
fact: «Corrugated iron» and «corrugated cardboard» are made this way, so they are stronger than a flat sheet.
fact: In Australia, a «corrugated road» is a dirt road with bumpy ridges.
fact: Corrugated can also mean wrinkled into lines, like a frowning forehead.
fact: Corrugated is also the past form of the rare verb corrugate, which means to fold or wrinkle something into ridges.
exercise: «The shed roof was made of corrugated iron.» What is corrugated iron? | A soft kind of paper | *Metal shaped into ridges and grooves, so it is stronger | Iron that has been painted bright red | Flat, smooth metal with no pattern
exercise: «Dad's forehead was corrugated with worry.» What does corrugated mean here? | Covered in mud | Bright and loud | Smooth and shiny | *Wrinkled into lines, like a frown
exercise: Why are corrugated cardboard boxes stronger than flat card? | The card is painted, so it is harder | The card has holes in it | Boxes never need to be strong | *The ridges make the sheet stiffer and harder to bend
test: «The old truck rattled along the corrugated road.» In Australia, a corrugated road is a dirt road with what? | Smooth black tar | Painted white lines | Lots of traffic lights | *Bumpy ridges
test: Which word is the past form of the verb corrugate? | *Corrugated | Corrugate | Corrugating | Corrugates
exam: «The workers fixed corrugated plastic sheets onto the fence.» Corrugated plastic is used because it is what? | *Strong and stiff because of its ridges | Clear like glass | Heavy and fragile | Soft like a sponge
